>> title: Challah
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, jewish, eggs, honey, braided
>> counters: Bakery, Deli
>> aka: challa, hallah, egg bread, braided egg bread
>> pairs-with: chicken-noodle-soup
>> servings: 12
>> time: 4 hr
>> slack: narrow — proof only until the braid holds a fingerprint slowly; past that the six strands lose their definition and bake into one round bulge
>> step.1: stir, stand 10 min
>> step.2: beat in
>> step.3: add flour and salt, knead 10 min
>> step.4: cover, rise until doubled
>> step.5: braid six strands, proof 1 hour
>> step.6: brush, seed, bake 350°F 30 to 35 min

Stir @warm water{3/4%cup}(180 mL) with @honey{1/4%cup}(85 g) and @instant yeast{2 1/4%tsp}(7 g), then let stand ~{10%min}.

Beat @eggs{2%large}, @egg yolks{2%large}, and @vegetable oil{1/3%cup}(75 mL) into @&(~1)yeast mixture{}.

Add @bread flour{4 1/4%cup}(570 g) and @table salt{2%tsp}(12 g) to @&(~1)egg mixture{}, then knead ~{10%min}.

Cover @&(~1)dough{} and rise until doubled, ~{1 1/2%hours}.

Braid @&(~1)dough{} into a six-strand loaf and proof ~{1%hour}.

Brush @&(~1)loaf{} with @beaten egg{1%large}, sprinkle with @sesame seeds{1%Tbs}, and bake at 350°F for ~{35%min}.
